# windows-win32-shim — Win32→m alias manifest (NDJSON)
#
# The single, versioned source of truth that drives the alias-object emitter
# (`alias_obj`, MW5-4) and its CLI (`gen-alias-obj`, MW5-5). The emitter writes a
# COFF object that redirects each genuine Win32 entry point to the shim's
# `m<Name>` export, with NO C++ compiler and NO MSVC tool involved — only the
# client's own linker consumes the result. See SHIM-D4.
#
# Format — NDJSON with a comment extension:
#   * One JSON object per ACTIVE alias, e.g.
#       {"win32":"RegOpenKeyExW","shim":"mRegOpenKeyExW"}
#     - "win32" (required): the genuine Win32 name being redirected.
#     - "shim"  (optional): the target export; defaults to "m" + win32.
#     - "alias" (optional, default true): set false to document a name that is
#       EXPORTED but deliberately NOT auto-redirected (opt-out; see CloseHandle —
#       redirecting every CloseHandle in a client would capture non-shim OS
#       handles).
#   * A blank line, or a line whose first non-blank characters are `#` or `//`,
#     is a comment / section header and is ignored by the emitter.
#   * A name this crate does not yet export is carried as a COMMENTED-OUT record
#     (`# {"win32":...}`); enable it by deleting the leading `# ` once the entry
#     point lands. This mirrors windows_win32_shim.def's enable-by-uncommenting.
#
# Parity is enforced by a unit test: the ACTIVE aliased set here must equal the
# aliased set of windows_win32_shim.def. Changing the ACTIVE set is a breaking
# change for any consumer linking the generated alias object.

# ============================================================================
# Filesystem (mwinfile.rs)
# ============================================================================

# ---- Handle lifetime --------------------------------------------------------
{"win32":"CloseHandle","shim":"mCloseHandle","alias":false}

